Preserve the deferred subagent/branch/interactive exchange paths while the ordinary state refactor proceeds. Despite this node's historical migration name, this goal does not implement a new protocol or migrate pending interaction/operation state to UnlockedData. Use audit /05/01/04 to identify the existing permission/question, plugin, subagent inspector/control, branch-confirmation and asynchronous request/completion interfaces that must remain. The user will design and implement one backend-requested popup requiring a reply before generalizing that design.

Make only minimal compatibility adjustments needed by removal of ordinary bulk state transfers, preserving owner-bound identifiers, generations, path-free data, invocation lifetime, ordering, cancellation and backend permission decisions. No dirty flag grants authority or resolves a prompt. Do not introduce canonical pending-popup state, change action/response semantics or replace history-bearing frames. Inspector focus is not the active agent receiving next Enter. Local selection/layout/draft state stays tui-thread-owned in tui-specific code, without locks/UnlockedData.

Verify the preserved paths still work after surrounding changes with relevant subagent, branch, plugin, permission/question and terminal regression tests. Document exact retained contracts/dependencies for the final boundary audit. Partial removal or an unimplemented backend endpoint requires explicit agreement on the affected feature and safe unsupported behavior; the default is preservation, not stubbing. Independently exposed ordinary active-agent/model/directory/token facts must use the new path without requiring the deferred exchanges to be rewritten.

Preserve image/editor/Mermaid service APIs and their existing synchronization as well; service capability/authority is not a local rendering preference. Do not snapshot SessionStore, permission/question queues, plugin endpoints/invocations, SubagentInspectorFrame, branch-confirmation operations, agent instructions or assembled prompts. /models and /scoped-models remain on-demand popups with their existing selection/toggle/reorder/save flows, not new ordinary catalog subscriptions. A canceled local candidate/preview must not mutate canonical selection.

Keep the existing ava::frontend registration and typed canonical-object initialization; FrontendDataIndices, SessionFrontendBinding and index-only initialization remain deferred, not prerequisites for compatibility work. Existing projections expose formatted strings, with typed access only for the established or separately demonstrated cross-projection calculation. Distinguish GitBranch's observed string from branch-confirmation protocols: preserve its existing backend observation cadence without watchers or render-time filesystem reads. Do not reopen /03's primary-selection policy: "none" is the accepted canonical no-configured-primary value, not a frontend-invented label for another configured agent.
